  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-02-26T13:26:21.731Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I instantly miss torso leaning (I have a lot of short-armed avatars). This is the one thing I feel that the old VRC IK, despite its faults, got right compared with other VRSNS applications. I do not like the sensation of my hands disconnecting from my avatars'. It \"feels\" odd, and is immersion-breaking.\nMeanwhile I am easily fooled into believing that I am rotating my torso a little despite not actually doing so IRL\nCould Torso leaning be an option for the new IK? That or automatic rescaling of arm length.",
